<div class="mt-10" id="topic-logical-operations">

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">
        5. Logical Operations
    </h2>

    <div class="w-full h-[1px] flex items-center justify-center pt-[10px]">
        <div class="bg-gray-600 w-full h-[1px]"></div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Logical operations apply connectives to propositions to create compound propositions. Evaluate each part using the truth-value rules for its connective.</p>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Evaluating a Compound Proposition</h3><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Consider the expression \((p \land q) \lor ¬ p\).</p><div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4"><table class="w-full text-center border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560] text-white"><th class="p-3">\(p\)</th><th class="p-3">\(q\)</th><th class="p-3">\(p \land q\)</th><th class="p-3">\(¬ p\)</th><th class="p-3">\((p \land q) \lor ¬ p\)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">T</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">F</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-[#3A2560]"><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">T</td></tr><tr><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">F</td><td class="p-3">T</td><td class="p-3">T</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-6">Order of Evaluation</h3><p class="text-md text-gray-400 px-3 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Unless parentheses indicate otherwise, a common order is:</p><ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2"><li>Parentheses and grouping symbols</li><li>Negation \(¬\)</li><li>Conjunction \(\land\)</li><li>Disjunction \(\lor\)</li><li>Implication \(→\)</li><li>Biconditional \(\leftrightarrow\)</li></ol><p class="text-gray-400">Use parentheses whenever the intended grouping could be unclear. Follow your instructor's convention if it differs.</p>
</div>
